CORE
main.c
--unwind 3 --rounds 3 --por --allow-pointer-unsoundness --array-rf
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
--
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
--
The array is declined without the change (used as a whole object), and the
verdict is the same either way; what this checks is that taking it keeps the
reads constrained. A merge taken as a havoc of the array fails here, at a[0].
See array_rf_merge_heap_violation for the other direction.
